# No Cursor commit attribution

This is a hard rule. The user has demanded it repeatedly.

- NEVER add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: cursoragent@cursor.com`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any Cursor attribution trailer to commits, PRs, or commit messages.
- NEVER pass `--trailer` related to Cursor when running `git commit`.
- After every `git commit` or `git commit --amend`, immediately run `git log -1 --format=%B` and verify there is no Cursor co-author / Made-with line.
- If a trailer was injected anyway (Cursor sometimes appends it outside hooks), rebuild the commit with `git commit-tree` so the tip has a clean message, then force-push only if the user already asked to rewrite/push that commit.
- Do not ask the user to clean it up. Fix it yourself before reporting success.
